@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+# Built-in test outputs
+
+The built-in runner can declare output directories through the public test
+orchestrator API and export their materialized locations after native tests.
+Existing commands retain their behavior when these options are absent.
+
+```sh
+buck2 test //example:test -- --output-env CAPTURES=images --outputs-manifest /tmp/outputs.bin
+```
+
+Each `--output-env ENV=relative-directory` sets that test environment variable
+to a declared output directory. The directory is pre-created and the runner
+requests local materialization, including after remote execution and cache
+hits. Names must be valid environment identifiers. Directory paths must be
+relative, nonempty, and contain no traversal or platform-specific separators.
+Repeated environment names or directory names are errors.
+
+`--outputs-manifest PATH` writes UTF-8 records framed with NUL bytes. The first
+field is `buck2-test-outputs-v1`. Every remaining record has four fields:
+the exact reported test target, actual test status, declared output name,
+and absolute retained local path. Records sort by target and output name.
+A test with no outputs has empty output name and path fields. A cancelled
+execution records `OMITTED`; execution results retain their `PASS`, `FAIL`,
+or `TIMEOUT` status. Unexpected remote-only output references are errors.
+No field can contain NUL. Tabs, newlines, and Unicode remain literal data.
+
+The runner copies public `ExecutionResult2.outputs` while their materialization
+lease is live into a fresh sibling directory `PATH.d`. That directory must not
+already exist; the runner never removes or overwrites a previous output tree.
+Only regular files and directories are accepted; symlinks and special files
+are errors. Consumers may stage the retained paths after the native command
+without inspecting internal output layouts or caches. Failure artifacts remain outputs
+of that test execution; retaining them does not make a failing test pass.
